  VT/TC Status Timeouts : 0
  TC errors             : 0
  CF evictions survived : 235
  drp / tcq             : 0 (see PART C)

Note on a misleading metric: this run logged ZERO "NACK-ing PGN request for
PGN 60928" lines, which initially looked like the roll-calls had simply
stopped. That proxy is wrong -- a BROADCAST roll-call is never NACKed, only
a request addressed specifically to us is. The 235 evictions prove the prune
cycle was running throughout. Prune activity, not NACK count, is the correct
measure.

Pre/post comparison (evictions in window vs. whether our partner was lost):
  pre-patch, New Holland alone (healthy)      0 evictions  -- no prunes ran
  pre-patch, InCommand alone (healthy)       23 evictions  -- survived on timing
  pre-patch, dual VT (failing)               62 evictions  -- partner lost
  pre-patch, NH disabled (failing, ~3s)       6 evictions  -- partner lost
  POST-PATCH, NH disabled, 800s             235 evictions  -- ZERO losses

