KEY READINGS:
  * TC-GEO (with pos) = Y. The terminal SUPPORTS TC-GEO with position. With a
    task active and an AB line selected it still sends 0 Value Commands and
    0 Value Requests. This kills the Session 3 TC-GEO licensing theory, and
    is strictly worse than Session 3's Trimble, which at least issued 2 Value
    Requests proving it had parsed our DDOP.
  * XTE decode reads the WRONG VENDOR'S PAYLOAD. Ground truth taken live from
    the Ag Leader screen went 144 -> 8 -> 118 -> 14 cm while our decoded value
    took only two values in ~400 samples (-144.65 and -142.09, i.e. val 3070
    and 3582) with xteAge ~57ms throughout. The field is frozen.
    Root cause: PGN 0xFFFF is manufacturer-proprietary and overloaded.
    Session 1 added SA 0x80 (Ag Leader/Raven) as an accepted sender for the
    JOHN DEERE decoder, assuming a shared layout. It is not shared -- we read
    John Deere byte offsets (data[3..4]) out of an Ag Leader message.
    Same cause explains quality byte 0x03 failing (d[1] & 0xF0) == 0x10 ->
    Quality 0, IsRtkQuality=N: d[1] is not a John Deere quality byte here.
    NOTE, recorded as a caution: an intermediate analysis concluded this was
    a 100x scale error, because (val-32000)/200 yields -144.65 cm against a
    measured 144 cm -- a near-perfect match on a SINGLE data point. The
    subsequent readings disproved it. One matching point was never enough.
    Fix requires a raw 8-byte capture of PGN 65535 from SA 0x80 against
    ground truth, then deriving the Ag Leader layout. Note this session also
    counted only 1x PGN 129283 and 3x PGN 60160, so neither standard NMEA2000
    XTE nor the Trimble legacy PGN is a usable alternative source here.
  * Lat/Lon still 0.000000 -- Session 1 bug #6, still open.
  * "last ... ms ago" for AISO/DDI equals board uptime, i.e. those timestamps
    are never set. Cosmetic, but worth a look.
